# Social Engineering Research

## Overview

This research focuses on social engineering threats and approaches
to improving cybersecurity awareness.

## Research Area

- Cybersecurity
- Social Engineering
- Human Factors
- Cybersecurity Awareness

## Publication

**Title:** Development of an Interactive, Educational Site to Counter Social Engineering

**Author:** Valeriia Yahlo

**Year:** 2025

## Abstract

**Core Goal**: To design and implement a lightweight, accessible, fully Ukrainian-language 
interactive web resource that educates non-technical users on social engineering techniques 
and tests their knowledge to improve digital hygiene
**Structure & Technologies**:
*Architecture*: Developed entirely on client-side technologies (HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript) 
as a single-page application (SPA) requiring no registration, back-end servers, or external databases.
*Key Sections*:
1. Theory: Concepts, principles, attack vectors (phishing, vishing, smishing, baiting, spear phishing, whaling), 
and target demographics.
2. Quiz/Testing: A 10-question test featuring interactive verification, automatic score calculation, visual 
color feedback (green/red), and targeted hints referencing theoretical modules.
3. Cheat Sheet: Key practical tips and an interactive table displaying user survey statistics on social engineering awareness.


